age":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.20513167238333285,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05267505983967813,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":69.6,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.043933805227226785,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":5e-05,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Barclays PLC provides various financial services in the United Kingdom, Europe, the Americas, Africa, the Middle East, and Asia. The company operates through Barclays UK; Barclays UK Corporate Bank; Barclays Private Bank and Wealth Management; Barclays Investment Bank; and Barclays US Consumer Bank segments. It offers financial services, such as current accounts, savings accounts, mortgages and unsecured lending, such as credit cards and loans retail banking, wholesale banking, investment banking, wealth management, and investment management services, as well as lending products. In addition, the company engages in securities dealing activities and issuing of credit cards. The company was formerly known as Barclays Bank public limited company and changed its name to Barclays PLC in January 1985. Barclays PLC was founded in 1690 and is headquartered in London, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Coimbatore Sundararajan Venkatakrishnan Ph.D. | Group CEO & Executive Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $7.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 93K people. Revenue per employee of $158K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $240K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 47\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Barclays PLC is a large-cap financial services business with a $76.0B market cap on $14.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are contracting by -20.3pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","The business throws off $22.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 152 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.60\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -20.3pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 53% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 86% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Truist hires Michael Stillman, Barclays to cut 200 jobs","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/truist-hires-michael-stillman-barclays-203000912.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794601800.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dr. Martens (LSE:DOCS) Stock Fair Value Moves Lower After Cautious Analyst Revisions","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dr-martens-lse-docs-stock-231037443.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794611437.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.828,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Oklo (NYSE:OKLO) Shares Up 3.3% \u2013 Still a Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/oklo-nyseoklo-shares-up-3-3-still-a-buy.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794606770.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":